.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Raw downloads are located, never copied -- see budget_tune/companion.py.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is not cosmetic: an unanchored "data/" matches a
# directory of that name at *any* depth, so it silently excluded budget_tune/data/ -- the
# package holding the leave-two-out split, the deduplication and the leakage guard. A clone
# would have failed to import, and nothing here would have said why.
/data/

# Results are committed deliberately, per study, so tables can be regenerated from
# artifacts. Lock files and in-progress checkpoints are not.
#
# The partial pattern matches the whole suffix: the campaign's checkpoints are named
# "search_runs.partial.jsonl", and a "*.partial" rule does not match them.
results/**/.measure.lock
results/**/*.partial.jsonl

# Operational logs, matching the sibling project. They are truncated on every launch, so
# they are not durable provenance anyway -- the failures worth keeping are written up in
# docs/campaign-history.md, which is committed.
results/*.log
results/**/*.log

# No AI tooling artifacts in the repository.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Session briefs and handoff notes written for coding agents. They are working notes about
# how to drive the work, not part of it, and they quote intermediate numbers that go stale
# the moment an artifact is regenerated. Ignored by pattern rather than by remembering to
# exclude each one, because a single `git add -A` is all it takes.
docs/claude-code-*.md
